        "original_id": "ebfc9341-94a1-524d-91f3-bd3ceefe83f5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: The Lost Tomb of Jesus documentary, Jerusalem ossuary discovery\n- People: Jesus, Mary Magdalene, Judah\n- Concepts: Ossuaries, secondary burial\n- Places: Jerusalem\n\nFacts:\n- In 1980, ossuaries were discovered in Jerusalem.\n- The 2007 documentary \"The Lost Tomb of Jesus\" proposed that inscriptions on ossuaries found in Jerusalem in 1980 were evidence that Jesus was married to Mary Magdalene and that their son was named Judah.\n- An ossuary is a chest, box, building, well, or site intended to serve as the final resting place of human skeletal remains.\n- In secondary burial, a body is first buried in a temporary grave, and after some years the skeletal remains are removed and placed in an ossuary.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6e5d3a3c-f2d8-578c-a5cd-e489cac7a50c",
        "text": "Page: Jesus bloodline. Sentence: The 2007 documentary \"The Lost Tomb of Jesus\" proposed that evidence existed to show that Jesus was married to Mary Magdalene and that their son was named Judah, based upon inscriptions found on ossuaries discovered in Jerusalem in 1980.\nPage: Ossuary. Sentence: An ossuary is a chest, box, building, well, or site made to serve as the final resting place of human skeletal remains.\nPage: Ossuary. Sentence: A body is first buried in a temporary grave, then after some years the skeletal remains are removed and placed in an ossuary.",
